      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-144436",
      ":question/problem": "$f(x) = \\frac{e^{x} - 1}{x^{4} - \\sin x}$\n\nThe function $f(x)$ has discontinuities at $a = 0$ and $b \\approx 0.95$. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $lim_(x \u2192 a^{-})f(x) = - \u221e$\n2. $lim_(x \u2192 b^{-})f(x) = - \u221e$\n3. $lim_(x \u2192 b^{+})f(x) = - \u221e$\n\n> A graphing calculator is required to answer this question."
